"They only want you to stand on being Black if you're going to be a Democrat."

Rep. Byron Donalds calls out the media for ignoring the historic possibilities of Florida and Michigan having their first Black governors just because both candidates are Republicans.

@ByronDonalds agreeing with the sentiment shared by @NICKIMINAJ , saying if he and Rep. John James were Democrats then their campaigns would be celebrated by the media.

“If myself or John were running as Democrats... every news outlet in the country would talk about how historic it is,” Donalds told @HARRISFAULKNER 

Reacting to Minaj’s post, Donalds says Black voters should pay attention to how conservative candidates are treated, arguing their historic campaigns would be celebrated if they were on the other side.

